ios: minimap zoom

For the mobile HUD's minimap zoom slider: setMinimapZoom(zoom) draws the minimap at `zoom` times its pixels per tile,
0.75..2 (1 = upstream, 4 px per tile; further out the map would reach past the black margin of the minimap image, as
the player can stand 16 tiles from its edge). The anti-macro wobble (macroMinimapZoom) stays on top. The map, the
dots, the hint arrow and a tap on the map (minimapLoop) all use the zoomed scale, and the dots' range and the arrow's
switch to a plain dot are measured on the map. hudState() reports minimapZoom. Unzoomed, nothing changes.

